    "body": "## Summary\n\nFinal commit of ADR-048. Marks the ADR as Implemented with the honest **zero-first-viewport-delta** caveat.\n\n## The delta (honest accounting)\n\n**Zero first-viewport delta.** Two independent conditions unmet:\n\n1. **`.mw-header` absent from current fetched HTML** — exact-class DOM walk: `mw-header NOT FOUND`. Rule exists in CSS, no element matches in current snapshot.\n2. **At viewport ≥ 1680px, `.mw-header` is `display: grid`** — the `@media (min-width: 1680px)` override wins. Flex only applies below 1680px; test viewport is 1774px.\n\nThe 3 wrap rules in Wikipedia CSS all target `.mw-header` variants. Until both conditions are met, flex-wrap produces no visible change.\n\n**Verification is synthetic-DOM only.** Same category as ADR-041 Commit 1 and ADR-047.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### Commit 1 — Refactor (byte-identical)\n\nExtracted `resolve_flex_line()` helper from `layout_flex_children`. Phases B–E (grow/shrink distribution, justify positioning, per-item layout, cross alignment) moved into the helper.\n\n- Single call site for `nowrap` preserves byte-identical output\n- All 598 pre-existing tests pass unchanged, including all 20 ADR-029 flex tests\n- 2307 assertions unchanged (not one fewer, not one more)\n\n### Commit 2 — Multi-line wrap\n\n- Flex dispatch reads `flex-wrap` (default `nowrap`)\n- `do_wrap = (flex-wrap == \"wrap\") && is_row`\n- `!do_wrap` branch: identical to ADR-029 pre-refactor code\n- `do_wrap` branch: greedy line-breaking, per-line `resolve_flex_line`, line stacking with `gap` fallback\n- 13 synthetic-DOM tests: wrap scenarios, regressions, per-line justify/align\n\n### Commit 3 — Docs (this commit)\n\n- ADR-048 → Implemented with zero-delta caveat\n- Post-ADR-048 note in ADR-029 (flex-wrap deferral closed)\n- README row + CHANGELOG entry\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-048: 598 cases / 2307 assertions\n- After Commit 1: unchanged (refactor)\n- After Commit 2: 611 cases / 2386 assertions (+13 / +79)\n- After Commit 3: unchanged (docs only)\n\n## Session's fifth category (still intact)\n\n| Category | Example | PNG check |\n|---|---|---|\n| **PNG-verified (first-viewport)** | ADR-042, ADR-043 | yes |\n| **PNG-verified (scroll)** | ADR-045 | yes |\n| **Behaviorally-complete, visually-subtle** | ADR-044 | caveat |\n| **Behaviorally-complete, visually-zero** | ADR-047, **ADR-048** | caveat (no consumer) |\n| **Deferred with reason** | ADR-041 Commit 2 | N/A |\n\n## Why this cycle ships\n\n- **Refactor proven byte-identical** — 598 tests unchanged after Commit 1\n- **Multi-line algorithm correct** — 13 synthetic tests pass\n- **Zero regression surface** — `!do_wrap` mirrors pre-ADR-048 exactly\n- **Future-ready** — the moment `.mw-header` appears in HTML AND viewport < 1680px, wrap works with zero code change\n- **ADR-029's biggest deferral closed**\n\n## Deferred (per ADR)\n\n- `align-content` (parsing + cross-axis distribution)\n- `flex-wrap: wrap-reverse` (0 uses)\n- `flex-direction: column` + wrap (0 uses)\n- Cross-axis shrink (CSS §9.3)\n- `gap: <a> <b>` two-value cross-axis interpretation\n\nRefs #227\n",
